{
  "_README": [
    "Single source of truth for the KV pre-push gate thresholds.",
    "",
    "`min` is the gate floor: a measured value BELOW it fails the gate.",
    "`known_good` is the reference run the floor was derived from (min ~= 95% of it).",
    "",
    "RULES:",
    "  1. A floor is NEVER lowered to make a run pass. A miss is diagnosed.",
    "  2. A floor may be ratcheted UP off a recorded multi-run session, and the",
    "     new number recorded with the runs behind it.",
    "  3. `min` is stored explicitly, not computed, so a change to the tolerance",
    "     constant can never silently move a shipped floor. check_baselines.py",
    "     warns if a `min` drifts from 95% of its `known_good` by more than 1 RPS.",
    "",
    "Mac and Linux tables are NOT interchangeable: EPYC 8124P @ 2.45 GHz produces",
    "~30% of Mac M-series KV throughput at parity (clock + IPC), and Naples- vs",
    "Milan-class chips flip the io_uring/epoll crossover at P=1 (doc/epoll_vs_iouring.md)."
  ],
  "tolerance": 0.95,
